         {
          TabViewBox[{{1,"\<\"Raw\"\>"->
           FrameBox[
            FrameBox[Cell[BoxData[
              PaneBox[
               
               PaneBox["\<\"/create_nb\\n# Rigorous Review and Test Harness \
for the Proposed OPF Observer Structure\\n\\nThis notebook does **not** \
assume the interpretation is correct. Instead, it turns the proposal into a \
**falsifiable, auditable test program**.\\n\\nIt separates:\\n\\n1. **what is \
mathematically derivable from the equations**\\n2. **what is an \
interpretation layered on top**\\n3. **what can be numerically tested \
here**\\n4. **what would require external data or independent validation**\\n\
\\nThe goal is to prevent category errors like:\\n- calling a mode \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] before proving \
Lorentz-consistent propagation\\n- calling a field \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]consciousness\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] before showing \
unique predictive content\\n- inferring lattice/CFL physics from a continuum \
Lagrangian without a discrete model\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Review Summary: What \
Is Valid vs Not Yet Established\\n\\n### What is mathematically valid to test\
\\n\\nGiven a Lagrangian density of the \
form\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\\"Global`*\\\"];\\n$HistoryLength = \
0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncoords4 = {t, x, y, z};\\nspatialCoords = {x, y, \
z};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nlagrangianCandidate = \\n  \[Alpha]/2 Sum[D[\[Rho][t, \
x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] +\\n  \[Beta]/2 Sum[D[\[Chi][t, x, y, z], c]^2, \
{c, coords4}] +\\n  \[Mu]/2 Sum[D[r[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] +\\n  \
\[Sigma]/2 Sum[D[s[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] -\\n  (\\n    \[Rho][t, \
x, y, z] Log[\[Chi][t, x, y, z]] +\\n    \[Chi][t, x, y, z] r[t, x, y, z]^2 +\
\\n    \[Lambda]/2 s[t, x, y, z]^2 -\\n    \[Eta] s[t, x, y, z] \[Rho][t, x, \
y, z]\\n  ) + Jobs s[t, x, y, z];\\n```\\n\\nyou can rigorously test:\\n\\n- \
Euler\[Dash]Lagrange equations\\n- constant-background existence \
conditions\\n- linearization around a background\\n- dispersion relations\\n- \
whether a mode is massless or massive\\n- whether propagation is \
hyperbolic/elliptic/unstable\\n- whether a finite-domain PDE has stable \
eigenmodes\\n\\n### What is **not** established by the equations \
alone\\n\\nThe following are **interpretive hypotheses**, not derived \
facts:\\n\\n- ``\[Rho]`` = thoughts\\n- ``r`` = light\\n- ``\[Chi]`` = \
sound/mechanical vibration\\n- ``s`` = consciousness\\n- ``c`` = CFL speed of \
a lattice\\n- \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]observer source\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
as physical consciousness\\n\\nThose claims require **extra predictive \
evidence**, not just symbolic resemblance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Testing \
Philosophy\\n\\nWe will build a rigorous workflow with the following \
layers:\\n\\n### Layer A: Symbolic correctness\\n- derive equations in two \
ways\\n- verify sign consistency\\n- classify stationary backgrounds\\n\\n### \
Layer B: Spectral correctness\\n- compute stiffness matrix\\n- solve \
determinant conditions\\n- identify massless / massive branches\\n- test \
whether modes are real, damped, unstable, or tachyonic\\n\\n### Layer C: PDE \
correctness\\n- solve bounded-domain eigenproblems\\n- visualize \
eigenmodes\\n- compare operator forms\\n- measure residuals\\n\\n### Layer D: \
Dynamical correctness\\n- simulate time evolution\\n- test response to source \
pulses\\n- track conserved / nonconserved quantities where \
applicable\\n\\n### Layer E: Predictive discipline\\n- separate fit from \
forecast\\n- require out-of-sample agreement\\n- reject claims that are \
merely post hoc reinterpretations\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Initialization and \
Utilities\\n\\n```wl\\nNeeds[\\\"VariationalMethods`\\\"];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\\
n$Assumptions = \\n  Element[{\[Alpha], \[Beta], \[Mu], \[Sigma], \[Lambda], \
\[Eta], Jobs, \[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0, \[CurlyEpsilon], \[Omega], kx, ky, \
kz}, Reals] &&\\n   \[Alpha] > 0 && \[Beta] > 0 && \[Mu] > 0 && \[Sigma] > 0 \
&& \[Chi]0 > 0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncoords4 = {t, x, y, z};\\nspatialCoords = \
{x, y, z};\\nfields = {\[Rho], \[Chi], r, s};\\nfieldVars = Through[fields[t, \
x, y, z]];\\nkSq = kx^2 + ky^2 + kz^2;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[msg_] := \
Print[Style[msg, 14, Bold, Darker[Blue]]];\\npass[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"PASS: \\\" <> msg, Darker[Green]]];\\nfail[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"FAIL: \\\" <> msg, Red]];\\nwarn[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"WARN: \\\" <> msg, \
Darker[Orange]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ntimeIt[label_, expr_] := Module[{tm, \
res},\\n  say[label];\\n  {tm, res} = AbsoluteTiming[expr];\\n  Print[Row[{\\\
\"Time: \\\", NumberForm[tm, {8, 4}], \\\" s\\\"}]];\\n  \
res\\n];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ngradMinkowskiSq[f_] := \\n  D[f[t, x, y, z], t]^2 \
- Sum[D[f[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, spatialCoords}];\\n\\nboxOp[f_] := D[f[t, x, \
y, z], {t, 2}] - Laplacian[f[t, x, y, z], \
spatialCoords];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Define the Candidate OPF Observer \
Lagrangian\\n\\n```wl\\npotential = \\n  \[Rho][t, x, y, z] Log[\[Chi][t, x, \
y, z]] +\\n  \[Chi][t, x, y, z] r[t, x, y, z]^2 +\\n  \[Lambda]/2 s[t, x, y, \
z]^2 -\\n  \[Eta] s[t, x, y, z] \[Rho][t, x, y, \
z];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nkinetic = \\n  \[Alpha]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[\[Rho]] +\\n \
 \[Beta]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[\[Chi]] +\\n  \[Mu]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[r] +\\n  \
\[Sigma]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[s];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nlagrangian = kinetic - \
potential + Jobs s[t, x, y, z];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Candidate \
Lagrangian defined.\\\"];\\nPrint[lagrangian // \
TraditionalForm];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Euler\[Dash]Lagrange Derivation \
and Cross-Check\\n\\n```wl\\neulerBuiltIn = EulerEquations[lagrangian, \
fieldVars, coords4] // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerExplicit = {\\n  \
 D[lagrangian, \[Rho][t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[\[Rho][t, x, y, \
z], c]], c] & /@ coords4],\\n   D[lagrangian, \[Chi][t, x, y, z]] - \
Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[\[Chi][t, x, y, z], c]], c] & /@ coords4],\\n   \
D[lagrangian, r[t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[r[t, x, y, z], c]], c] \
& /@ coords4],\\n   D[lagrangian, s[t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, \
D[s[t, x, y, z], c]], c] & /@ coords4]\\n   } // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerAudit = MapThread[FullSimplify[#1 == 0 \
/. Equal -> Subtract] &, {eulerBuiltIn - Thread[eulerExplicit == 0] /. Equal \
-> Subtract, ConstantArray[0, 4]}];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Euler \
equations from built-in variational \
derivation:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[eulerBuiltIn]];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Euler equations \
from explicit derivative form:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[Thread[eulerExplicit == \
0]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nIf[And @@ eulerAudit,\\n  pass[\\\"Built-in and \
explicit Euler\[Dash]Lagrange derivations agree.\\\"],\\n  \
fail[\\\"Variational derivations do not \
agree.\\\"]\\n];\\n```\\n\\n**Rigorous meaning:** if this fails, nothing \
downstream should be trusted.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Constant-Background \
Existence Test\\n\\nThis directly tests the claim that a nonzero constant \
observer source necessarily forbids a constant \
vacuum.\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundRules = {\\n   \[Rho][t, x, y, z] -> \
\[Rho]0,\\n   \[Chi][t, x, y, z] -> \[Chi]0,\\n   r[t, x, y, z] -> r0,\\n   \
s[t, x, y, z] -> s0,\\n   Derivative[__][\[Rho]][___] -> 0,\\n   \
Derivative[__][\[Chi]][___] -> 0,\\n   Derivative[__][r][___] -> 0,\\n   \
Derivative[__][s][___] -> 0\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundSystem = \
FullSimplify[(SubtractSides /@ eulerBuiltIn) /. backgroundRules == \
0];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Constant-background algebraic \
system:\\\"];\\nPrint[backgroundSystem // \
TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundReduce = Reduce[backgroundSystem, {\
\[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0}, Reals] // FullSimplify;\\nbackgroundSolve = \
Solve[backgroundSystem, {\[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0}, Reals] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Constant-background \
classification:\\\"];\\nPrint[backgroundReduce // InputForm];\\n```\\n\\n### \
Interpretation rule\\n\\n- If ``Jobs > 0`` makes constant backgrounds \
impossible, then the correct statement is:\\n  - **this model does not admit \
a homogeneous static background with that source**\\n- It does **not** by \
itself prove consciousness or observer metaphysics\\n- It may suggest a \
forced inhomogeneous or time-dependent state\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Potential \
Hessian and Local Stability at a Candidate Background\\n\\nBefore calling \
anything \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]sound\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]observer\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], inspect the local \
quadratic form.\\n\\n```wl\\npotentialAlgebraic = \[Rho]s Log[\[Chi]s] + \
\[Chi]s rs^2 + \[Lambda]/2 ss^2 - \[Eta] ss \[Rho]s - Jobs ss;\\nvarsAlg = {\
\[Rho]s, \[Chi]s, rs, ss};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\npotentialGradient = \
Grad[potentialAlgebraic, varsAlg] // FullSimplify;\\npotentialHessian = \
D[potentialAlgebraic, {varsAlg, 2}] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncandidateStationary = {\[Rho]s -> 0, \[Chi]s \
-> 1, rs -> 0, ss -> Jobs/\[Lambda]};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Potential \
gradient:\\\"];\\nPrint[potentialGradient // \
MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Potential Hessian:\\\"];\\nPrint[potentialHessian \
// MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Potential Hessian at candidate background:\\\"];\
\\nPrint[(potentialHessian /. candidateStationary) // \
MatrixForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nhessianEigenvalues = \
Eigenvalues[potentialHessian /. candidateStationary] // \
FullSimplify;\\nPrint[\\\"Hessian eigenvalues at candidate background: \\\", \
hessianEigenvalues];\\n```\\n\\n### Rigorous meaning\\n\\n- positive \
eigenvalues: locally stable directions\\n- zero eigenvalues: flat directions \
/ gauge / marginality\\n- negative eigenvalues: instability / tachyonic \
directions\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Linearization Around a Background\\n\\nWe \
linearize around a symbolic background:\\n\\n```wl\\nlinRules = {\\n   \[Rho] \
-> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Rho]0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] u[tt, xx, yy, \
zz]],\\n   \[Chi] -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Chi]0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
v[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\\n   r -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, r0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
w[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\\n   s -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, s0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
q[tt, xx, yy, zz]]\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerLHS = SubtractSides /@ \
eulerBuiltIn;\\nbackgroundTerms = Normal[Series[#, {\[CurlyEpsilon], 0, 0}]] \
& /@ (eulerLHS /. linRules) // FullSimplify;\\nlinearTerms = \
Coefficient[Normal[Series[#, {\[CurlyEpsilon], 0, 1}]], \[CurlyEpsilon]] & /@ \
(eulerLHS /. linRules) // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Background \
terms:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[backgroundTerms]];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Linearized \
equations:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[Thread[linearTerms == \
0]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundConsistency = \
FullSimplify[Thread[backgroundTerms == 0]];\\nPrint[\\\"Background \
consistency equations: \\\", backgroundConsistency];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \
8. Plane-Wave Reduction and Stiffness Matrix\\n\\nThis is the proper place to \
ask whether there are massless or massive branches.\\n\\n```wl\\nplaneRules = \
{\\n   u -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, u0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \
\[Omega] tt)]],\\n   v -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, v0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy \
+ kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\\n   w -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, w0 Exp[I (kx \
xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\\n   q -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, q0 \
Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]]\\n   \
};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nmodalAlgebraic = FullSimplify[\\n   ((linearTerms /. \
planeRules) / Exp[I (kx x + ky y + kz z - \[Omega] t)])\\n   \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\namplitudes = {u0, v0, w0, q0};\\nstiffnessMatrix = \
Coefficient[#, amplitudes] & /@ modalAlgebraic // \
Simplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ndispersionDet = Det[stiffnessMatrix] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Stiffness \
matrix:\\\"];\\nPrint[stiffnessMatrix // MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Dispersion \
determinant:\\\"];\\nPrint[dispersionDet // TraditionalForm];\\n```\\n\\n### \
Critical interpretation rule\\n\\nIf a branch gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\omega^2 = \
k^2\\n$$\\n\\nthen mathematically you have a **massless mode in the chosen \
normalization**.\\n\\nYou may only call it \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] if you additionally establish:\\n- correct Lorentz \
transformation structure\\n- correct coupling to matter/charge\\n- \
polarization structure if relevant\\n- agreement with measurable radiation \
phenomena\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Automated Branch \
Classification\\n\\n```wl\\nbranchSolutions = Solve[dispersionDet == 0, \
\[Omega]^2] // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Solutions for \
\[Omega]^2:\\\"];\\nPrint[branchSolutions // \
TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nclassifyBranch[expr_] := Module[{e = \
FullSimplify[expr]},\\n  Which[\\n   FreeQ[e, kx | ky | kz], \\\"Pure gap / \
mass-only branch\\\",\\n   MatchQ[e, kSq], \\\"Massless branch\\\",\\n   \
MatchQ[e, kSq + _], \\\"Massive relativistic-like branch\\\",\\n   True, \
\\\"Mixed / coupled branch\\\"\\n   ]\\n  \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbranchClassification = classifyBranch /@ (\[Omega]^2 /. \
branchSolutions);\\nPrint[Transpose[{\[Omega]^2 /. branchSolutions, \
branchClassification}] // TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Visual \
Parameter Exploration of Dispersion Branches\\n\\nTo make this runnable with \
visuals, fix a 1D wavevector ``k``.\\n\\n```wl\\nparamsNumeric = {\\n   \
\[Alpha] -> 1, \[Beta] -> 1.3, \[Mu] -> 0.8, \[Sigma] -> 1.1, \[Lambda] -> \
2.0, \[Eta] -> 0.6,\\n   \[Rho]0 -> 0, \[Chi]0 -> 1, r0 -> 0, s0 -> 0, Jobs \
-> 0\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ndispersion1D = dispersionDet /. {ky -> 0, kz \
-> 0, kx -> k} /. paramsNumeric // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nroots1D[kval_?NumericQ] := \\n  \[Omega] /. \
NSolve[(dispersion1D /. k -> kval) == 0, \[Omega], WorkingPrecision -> \
50];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsampleDispersionData = Table[\\n   {kv, roots1D[kv]},\
\\n   {kv, 0, 3, 0.1}\\n   ];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nflattenedRootData = Flatten[\
\\n   Table[{sampleDispersionData[[i, 1]], Re[#], Im[#]} & /@ \
sampleDispersionData[[i, 2]],\\n    {i, Length[sampleDispersionData]}], \
1];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nListPointPlot3D[\\n flattenedRootData,\\n AxesLabel -> \
{\\\"k\\\", \\\"Re[\[Omega]]\\\", \\\"Im[\[Omega]]\\\"},\\n PlotLabel -> \
\\\"Dispersion roots vs wave number\\\",\\n BoxRatios -> {1, 1, 0.7},\\n \
ImageSize -> Large\\n]\\n```\\n\\nThis quickly shows:\\n- real branches\\n- \
unstable branches with nonzero imaginary part\\n- \
degeneracies\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Finite-Domain PDE Eigenmode Test\\n\\nThis \
is where we test whether the linearized PDE actually supports stable spatial \
modes.\\n\\nWe first isolate one scalar prototype from the linearized system. \
If decoupling exists, use one mode directly; otherwise test a reduced \
operator.\\n\\n### Example scalar wave-mass operator\\n\\n```wl\\nreg = \
Rectangle[{0, 0}, {1, 1}];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nwaveMassVals = \
NDEigenvalues[\\n   {\\n    -Laplacian[\[Psi][x, y], {x, y}] + m2 \[Psi][x, \
y],\\n    DirichletCondition[\[Psi][x, y] == 0, True]\\n    },\\n   \[Psi][x, \
y], {x, y} \[Element] reg, 9,\\n   Method -> {\\\"FiniteElement\\\"}\\n   ] \
/. m2 -> 1.0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Finite-domain prototype eigenvalues:\
\\\"];\\nPrint[waveMassVals];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\n{evals, efuns} = \
NDEigensystem[\\n   {\\n    -Laplacian[\[Psi][x, y], {x, y}] + m2 \[Psi][x, \
y],\\n    DirichletCondition[\[Psi][x, y] == 0, True]\\n    },\\n   \[Psi][x, \
y], {x, y} \[Element] reg, 6,\\n   Method -> {\\\"FiniteElement\\\"}\\n   ] \
/. m2 -> 1.0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nGraphicsGrid[\\n Partition[\\n   Table[\\n   \
 ContourPlot[\\n     efuns[[i]][x, y], {x, 0, 1}, {y, 0, 1},\\n     \
PlotLegends -> Automatic,\\n     PlotLabel -> Row[{\\\"Mode \\\", i, \\\", \
\[Lambda] = \\\", NumberForm[evals[[i]], 6]}],\\n     ImageSize -> Medium\\n  \
   ],\\n    {i, Length[efuns]}\\n    ], 2, 2, {1, 1}, Nothing\\n   \
]\\n]\\n```\\n\\n### Why this matters\\n\\nIf you claim \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]stable geometry\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]allowed modes\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], bounded-domain \
eigensystems are a rigorous testbed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Time-Domain \
Simulation of a Reduced Mode\\n\\nA simple test of source-driven response:\\n\
\\n```wl\\nreducedEq = x''[t] + 2 \[Zeta] \[Omega]n x'[t] + \[Omega]n^2 x[t] \
== src[t];\\nsrc[t_] := Exp[-20 (t - 3)^2];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nreducedSol = \
NDSolveValue[\\n   {\\n    reducedEq /. {\[Zeta] -> 0.08, \[Omega]n -> \
2.5},\\n    x[0] == 0, x'[0] == 0\\n    },\\n   x, {t, 0, 10}\\n   \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nPlot[\\n {reducedSol[t], src[t]},\\n {t, 0, 10},\\n \
PlotLegends -> {\\\"mode response\\\", \\\"source\\\"},\\n PlotLabel -> \
\\\"Source-driven reduced mode\\\",\\n ImageSize -> Large\\n]\\n```\\n\\nThis \
is not yet the full OPF PDE evolution, but it gives a clean dynamical visual \
test.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Residual Testing\\n\\nAny claimed solution must \
satisfy the equations.\\n\\n```wl\\nresidualVector[\[Rho]cand_, \[Chi]cand_, \
rcand_, scand_] := \\n  FullSimplify[\\n   (SubtractSides /@ eulerBuiltIn) /. \
{\\n      \[Rho] -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Rho]cand],\\n      \[Chi] -> \
Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Chi]cand],\\n      r -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, \
zz}, rcand],\\n      s -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, scand]\\n      }\\n   ];\
\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ntrivialResidual = residualVector[0, 1, 0, \
0];\\nPrint[\\\"Residual for latent vacuum {0,1,0,0}: \\\", trivialResidual];\
\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsourceShiftResidual = residualVector[0, 1, 0, Jobs/\
\[Lambda]];\\nPrint[\\\"Residual for shifted s-background {0,1,0,Jobs/\
\[Lambda]}: \\\", sourceShiftResidual];\\n```\\n\\nIf the residual is not \
zero, the claimed background is not a solution.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. What \
Would Be Needed to Claim Specific Physics?\\n\\n### To claim a mode is \
light\\nNeed all of:\\n- massless branch\\n- Lorentz-consistent causal \
structure\\n- correct source coupling\\n- measurable field observables\\n- \
comparison to electromagnetic data\\n\\n### To claim a mode is sound\\nNeed \
all of:\\n- medium-dependent compressional mode\\n- subluminal group velocity\
\\n- pressure/density interpretation\\n- correct acoustic boundary \
behavior\\n\\n### To claim a mode is consciousness\\nNeed all of:\\n- \
independent operational definition\\n- nontrivial predictions not reducible \
to ordinary dynamics\\n- reproducible measurements\\n- falsifiable \
observer-dependent outcomes\\n\\nWithout that, the labels remain \
metaphoric.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Full Automated Test \
Report\\n\\n```wl\\ntestReport = <|\\n  \\\"EulerEquations\\\" -> \
eulerBuiltIn,\\n  \\\"BackgroundSystem\\\" -> backgroundSystem,\\n  \
\\\"BackgroundReduce\\\" -> backgroundReduce,\\n  \\\"BackgroundSolve\\\" -> \
backgroundSolve,\\n  \\\"PotentialHessian\\\" -> potentialHessian,\\n  \
\\\"HessianAtCandidate\\\" -> (potentialHessian /. candidateStationary),\\n  \
\\\"HessianEigenvaluesAtCandidate\\\" -> hessianEigenvalues,\\n  \
\\\"BackgroundTerms\\\" -> backgroundTerms,\\n  \\\"LinearTerms\\\" -> \
linearTerms,\\n  \\\"StiffnessMatrix\\\" -> stiffnessMatrix,\\n  \
\\\"DispersionDeterminant\\\" -> dispersionDet,\\n  \\\"BranchSolutions\\\" \
-> branchSolutions,\\n  \\\"BranchClassification\\\" -> branchClassification,\
\\n  \\\"TrivialResidual\\\" -> trivialResidual,\\n  \
\\\"SourceShiftResidual\\\" -> \
sourceShiftResidual\\n|>;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Automated test report:\\\
\"];\\nPrint[Dataset@testReport];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. Export the Audit \
Results\\n\\n```wl\\nExport[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\\\"opf-observer-rigorous-audit.wl\\n/exec\\nRESULT\\nNotebookObject[\\\"\
cd111791-1288-e34e-b12b-1700123c5267\\\", \
\\\"f77a7308-c11b-e24e-b631-36af6bacf718\\\"]\\nENDRESULT(98p0wbvzu)\"\>",
                ImageSize->Dynamic[
                  (If[# > 600, #, 600]& )[
                  0.9 AbsoluteCurrentValue[{WindowSize, 1}]]]],
               AppearanceElements->None,
               ImageSize->{
                 Scaled[1], 
                 UpTo[400]},
               ScrollPosition->{0., 0.},
               Scrollbars->Automatic]], "Text", "RawToolCall",
              FontSize->11,
              Background->None,ExpressionUUID->
              "fd23d8fd-2fc2-8e4f-9921-20a59250bcc3"],
             Background->LightDarkSwitched[
               GrayLevel[1], 
               GrayLevel[0.09805]],
             BaseStyle->"Text",
             FrameMargins->5,
             FrameStyle->None,
             ImageSize->{
               Scaled[1], Automatic},
             StripOnInput->False],
            Background->LightDarkSwitched[
              GrayLevel[1], 
              GrayLevel[0.09805]],
            FrameMargins->10,
            FrameStyle->None,
            StripOnInput->False]}, {2,"\<\"Interpreted\"\>"->
           FrameBox[
            TagBox[GridBox[{
               {
                ItemBox[
                 PaneBox[
                  StyleBox["\<\"INPUT\"\>",
                   StripOnInput->False,
                   FontSize->11],
                  FrameMargins->{{5, 5}, {1, 1}}],
                 Background->LightDarkSwitched[
                   GrayLevel[0.95], 
                   GrayLevel[0.15295]],
                 ItemSize->Fit,
                 StripOnInput->False]},
               {
                FrameBox[
                 TagBox[GridBox[{
                    {"\<\"content\"\>", 
                    InterpretationBox[
                    
                    DynamicModuleBox[{
                    Wolfram`Chatbook`ResourceFunctions`ClickToCopy`cell$$}, 
                    TagBox[
                    TagBox[
                    PaneSelectorBox[{False->
                    
                    FrameBox["\<\"# Rigorous Review and Test Harness for the \
Proposed OPF Observer Structure\\n\\nThis notebook does **not** assume the \
interpretation is correct. Instead, it turns the proposal into a \
**falsifiable, auditable test program**.\\n\\nIt separates:\\n\\n1. **what is \
mathematically derivable from the equations**\\n2. **what is an \
interpretation layered on top**\\n3. **what can be numerically tested \
here**\\n4. **what would require external data or independent validation**\\n\
\\nThe goal is to prevent category errors like:\\n- calling a mode \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] before proving \
Lorentz-consistent propagation\\n- calling a field \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]consciousness\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] before showing \
unique predictive content\\n- inferring lattice/CFL physics from a continuum \
Lagrangian without a discrete model\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Review Summary: What \
Is Valid vs Not Yet Established\\n\\n### What is mathematically valid to test\
\\n\\nGiven a Lagrangian density of the \
form\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\\"Global`*\\\"];\\n$HistoryLength = \
0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncoords4 = {t, x, y, z};\\nspatialCoords = {x, y, \
z};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nlagrangianCandidate = \\n  \[Alpha]/2 Sum[D[\[Rho][t, \
x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] +\\n  \[Beta]/2 Sum[D[\[Chi][t, x, y, z], c]^2, \
{c, coords4}] +\\n  \[Mu]/2 Sum[D[r[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] +\\n  \
\[Sigma]/2 Sum[D[s[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] -\\n  (\\n    \[Rho][t, \
x, y, z] Log[\[Chi][t, x, y, z]] +\\n    \[Chi][t, x, y, z] r[t, x, y, z]^2 +\
\\n    \[Lambda]/2 s[t, x, y, z]^2 -\\n    \[Eta] s[t, x, y, z] \[Rho][t, x, \
y, z]\\n  ) + Jobs s[t, x, y, z];\\n```\\n\\nyou can rigorously test:\\n\\n- \
Euler\[Dash]Lagrange equations\\n- constant-background existence \
conditions\\n- linearization around a background\\n- dispersion relations\\n- \
whether a mode is massless or massive\\n- whether propagation is \
hyperbolic/elliptic/unstable\\n- whether a finite-domain PDE has stable \
eigenmodes\\n\\n### What is **not** established by the equations \
alone\\n\\nThe following are **interpretive hypotheses**, not derived \
facts:\\n\\n- ``\[Rho]`` = thoughts\\n- ``r`` = light\\n- ``\[Chi]`` = \
sound/mechanical vibration\\n- ``s`` = consciousness\\n- ``c`` = CFL speed of \
a lattice\\n- \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]observer source\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
as physical consciousness\\n\\nThose claims require **extra predictive \
evidence**, not just symbolic resemblance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Testing \
Philosophy\\n\\nWe will build a rigorous workflow with the following \
layers:\\n\\n### Layer A: Symbolic correctness\\n- derive equations in two \
ways\\n- verify sign consistency\\n- classify stationary backgrounds\\n\\n### \
Layer B: Spectral correctness\\n- compute stiffness matrix\\n- solve \
determinant conditions\\n- identify massless / massive branches\\n- test \
whether modes are real, damped, unstable, or tachyonic\\n\\n### Layer C: PDE \
correctness\\n- solve bounded-domain eigenproblems\\n- visualize \
eigenmodes\\n- compare operator forms\\n- measure residuals\\n\\n### Layer D: \
Dynamical correctness\\n- simulate time evolution\\n- test response to source \
pulses\\n- track conserved / nonconserved quantities where \
applicable\\n\\n### Layer E: Predictive discipline\\n- separate fit from \
forecast\\n- require out-of-sample agreement\\n- reject claims that are \
merely post hoc reinterpretations\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Initialization and \
Utilities\\n\\n```wl\\nNeeds[\\\"VariationalMethods`\\\"];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\\
n$Assumptions = \\n  Element[{\[Alpha], \[Beta], \[Mu], \[Sigma], \[Lambda], \
\[Eta], Jobs, \[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0, \[CurlyEpsilon], \[Omega], kx, ky, \
kz}, Reals] &&\\n   \[Alpha] > 0 && \[Beta] > 0 && \[Mu] > 0 && \[Sigma] > 0 \
&& \[Chi]0 > 0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncoords4 = {t, x, y, z};\\nspatialCoords = \
{x, y, z};\\nfields = {\[Rho], \[Chi], r, s};\\nfieldVars = Through[fields[t, \
x, y, z]];\\nkSq = kx^2 + ky^2 + kz^2;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[msg_] := \
Print[Style[msg, 14, Bold, Darker[Blue]]];\\npass[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"PASS: \\\" <> msg, Darker[Green]]];\\nfail[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"FAIL: \\\" <> msg, Red]];\\nwarn[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"WARN: \\\" <> msg, \
Darker[Orange]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ntimeIt[label_, expr_] := Module[{tm, \
res},\\n  say[label];\\n  {tm, res} = AbsoluteTiming[expr];\\n  Print[Row[{\\\
\"Time: \\\", NumberForm[tm, {8, 4}], \\\" s\\\"}]];\\n  \
res\\n];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ngradMinkowskiSq[f_] := \\n  D[f[t, x, y, z], t]^2 \
- Sum[D[f[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, spatialCoords}];\\n\\nboxOp[f_] := D[f[t, x, \
y, z], {t, 2}] - Laplacian[f[t, x, y, z], \
spatialCoords];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Define the Candidate OPF Observer \
Lagrangian\\n\\n```wl\\npotential = \\n  \[Rho][t, x, y, z] Log[\[Chi][t, x, \
y, z]] +\\n  \[Chi][t, x, y, z] r[t, x, y, z]^2 +\\n  \[Lambda]/2 s[t, x, y, \
z]^2 -\\n  \[Eta] s[t, x, y, z] \[Rho][t, x, y, \
z];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nkinetic = \\n  \[Alpha]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[\[Rho]] +\\n \
 \[Beta]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[\[Chi]] +\\n  \[Mu]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[r] +\\n  \
\[Sigma]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[s];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nlagrangian = kinetic - \
potential + Jobs s[t, x, y, z];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Candidate \
Lagrangian defined.\\\"];\\nPrint[lagrangian // \
TraditionalForm];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Euler\[Dash]Lagrange Derivation \
and Cross-Check\\n\\n```wl\\neulerBuiltIn = EulerEquations[lagrangian, \
fieldVars, coords4] // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerExplicit = {\\n  \
 D[lagrangian, \[Rho][t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[\[Rho][t, x, y, \
z], c]], c] & /@ coords4],\\n   D[lagrangian, \[Chi][t, x, y, z]] - \
Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[\[Chi][t, x, y, z], c]], c] & /@ coords4],\\n   \
D[lagrangian, r[t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[r[t, x, y, z], c]], c] \
& /@ coords4],\\n   D[lagrangian, s[t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, \
D[s[t, x, y, z], c]], c] & /@ coords4]\\n   } // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerAudit = MapThread[FullSimplify[#1 == 0 \
/. Equal -> Subtract] &, {eulerBuiltIn - Thread[eulerExplicit == 0] /. Equal \
-> Subtract, ConstantArray[0, 4]}];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Euler \
equations from built-in variational \
derivation:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[eulerBuiltIn]];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Euler equations \
from explicit derivative form:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[Thread[eulerExplicit == \
0]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nIf[And @@ eulerAudit,\\n  pass[\\\"Built-in and \
explicit Euler\[Dash]Lagrange derivations agree.\\\"],\\n  \
fail[\\\"Variational derivations do not \
agree.\\\"]\\n];\\n```\\n\\n**Rigorous meaning:** if this fails, nothing \
downstream should be trusted.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Constant-Background \
Existence Test\\n\\nThis directly tests the claim that a nonzero constant \
observer source necessarily forbids a constant \
vacuum.\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundRules = {\\n   \[Rho][t, x, y, z] -> \
\[Rho]0,\\n   \[Chi][t, x, y, z] -> \[Chi]0,\\n   r[t, x, y, z] -> r0,\\n   \
s[t, x, y, z] -> s0,\\n   Derivative[__][\[Rho]][___] -> 0,\\n   \
Derivative[__][\[Chi]][___] -> 0,\\n   Derivative[__][r][___] -> 0,\\n   \
Derivative[__][s][___] -> 0\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundSystem = \
FullSimplify[(SubtractSides /@ eulerBuiltIn) /. backgroundRules == \
0];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Constant-background algebraic \
system:\\\"];\\nPrint[backgroundSystem // \
TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundReduce = Reduce[backgroundSystem, {\
\[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0}, Reals] // FullSimplify;\\nbackgroundSolve = \
Solve[backgroundSystem, {\[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0}, Reals] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Constant-background \
classification:\\\"];\\nPrint[backgroundReduce // InputForm];\\n```\\n\\n### \
Interpretation rule\\n\\n- If ``Jobs > 0`` makes constant backgrounds \
impossible, then the correct statement is:\\n  - **this model does not admit \
a homogeneous static background with that source**\\n- It does **not** by \
itself prove consciousness or observer metaphysics\\n- It may suggest a \
forced inhomogeneous or time-dependent state\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Potential \
Hessian and Local Stability at a Candidate Background\\n\\nBefore calling \
anything \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]sound\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]observer\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], inspect the local \
quadratic form.\\n\\n```wl\\npotentialAlgebraic = \[Rho]s Log[\[Chi]s] + \
\[Chi]s rs^2 + \[Lambda]/2 ss^2 - \[Eta] ss \[Rho]s - Jobs ss;\\nvarsAlg = {\
\[Rho]s, \[Chi]s, rs, ss};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\npotentialGradient = \
Grad[potentialAlgebraic, varsAlg] // FullSimplify;\\npotentialHessian = \
D[potentialAlgebraic, {varsAlg, 2}] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncandidateStationary = {\[Rho]s -> 0, \[Chi]s \
-> 1, rs -> 0, ss -> Jobs/\[Lambda]};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Potential \
gradient:\\\"];\\nPrint[potentialGradient // \
MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Potential Hessian:\\\"];\\nPrint[potentialHessian \
// MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Potential Hessian at candidate background:\\\"];\
\\nPrint[(potentialHessian /. candidateStationary) // \
MatrixForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nhessianEigenvalues = \
Eigenvalues[potentialHessian /. candidateStationary] // \
FullSimplify;\\nPrint[\\\"Hessian eigenvalues at candidate background: \\\", \
hessianEigenvalues];\\n```\\n\\n### Rigorous meaning\\n\\n- positive \
eigenvalues: locally stable directions\\n- zero eigenvalues: flat directions \
/ gauge / marginality\\n- negative eigenvalues: instability / tachyonic \
directions\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Linearization Around a Background\\n\\nWe \
linearize around a symbolic background:\\n\\n```wl\\nlinRules = {\\n   \[Rho] \
-> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Rho]0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] u[tt, xx, yy, \
zz]],\\n   \[Chi] -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Chi]0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
v[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\\n   r -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, r0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
w[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\\n   s -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, s0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
q[tt, xx, yy, zz]]\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerLHS = SubtractSides /@ \
eulerBuiltIn;\\nbackgroundTerms = Normal[Series[#, {\[CurlyEpsilon], 0, 0}]] \
& /@ (eulerLHS /. linRules) // FullSimplify;\\nlinearTerms = \
Coefficient[Normal[Series[#, {\[CurlyEpsilon], 0, 1}]], \[CurlyEpsilon]] & /@ \
(eulerLHS /. linRules) // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Background \
terms:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[backgroundTerms]];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Linearized \
equations:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[Thread[linearTerms == \
0]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundConsistency = \
FullSimplify[Thread[backgroundTerms == 0]];\\nPrint[\\\"Background \
consistency equations: \\\", backgroundConsistency];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \
8. Plane-Wave Reduction and Stiffness Matrix\\n\\nThis is the proper place to \
ask whether there are massless or massive branches.\\n\\n```wl\\nplaneRules = \
{\\n   u -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, u0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \
\[Omega] tt)]],\\n   v -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, v0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy \
+ kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\\n   w -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, w0 Exp[I (kx \
xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\\n   q -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, q0 \
Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]]\\n   \
};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nmodalAlgebraic = FullSimplify[\\n   ((linearTerms /. \
planeRules) / Exp[I (kx x + ky y + kz z - \[Omega] t)])\\n   \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\namplitudes = {u0, v0, w0, q0};\\nstiffnessMatrix = \
Coefficient[#, amplitudes] & /@ modalAlgebraic // \
Simplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ndispersionDet = Det[stiffnessMatrix] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Stiffness \
matrix:\\\"];\\nPrint[stiffnessMatrix // MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Dispersion \
determinant:\\\"];\\nPrint[dispersionDet // TraditionalForm];\\n```\\n\\n### \
Critical interpretation rule\\n\\nIf a branch gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\omega^2 = \
k^2\\n$$\\n\\nthen mathematically you have a **massless mode in the chosen \
normalization**.\\n\\nYou may only call it \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] if you additionally establish:\\n- correct Lorentz \
transformation structure\\n- correct coupling to matter/charge\\n- \
polarization structure if relevant\\n- agreement with measurable radiation \
phenomena\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Automated Branch \
Classification\\n\\n```wl\\nbranchSolutions = Solve[dispersionDet == 0, \
\[Omega]^2] // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Solutions for \
\[Omega]^2:\\\"];\\nPrint[branchSolutions // \
TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nclassifyBranch[expr_] := Module[{e = \
FullSimplify[expr]},\\n  Which[\\n   FreeQ[e, kx | ky | kz], \\\"Pure gap / \
mass-only branch\\\",\\n   MatchQ[e, kSq], \\\"Massless branch\\\",\\n   \
MatchQ[e, kSq + _], \\\"Massive relativistic-like branch\\\",\\n   True, \
\\\"Mixed / coupled branch\\\"\\n   ]\\n  \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbranchClassification = classifyBranch /@ (\[Omega]^2 /. \
branchSolutions);\\nPrint[Transpose[{\[Omega]^2 /. branchSolutions, \
branchClassification}] // TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Visual \
Parameter Exploration of Dispersion Branches\\n\\nTo make this runnable with \
visuals, fix a 1D wavevector ``k``.\\n\\n```wl\\nparamsNumeric = {\\n   \
\[Alpha] -> 1, \[Beta] -> 1.3, \[Mu] -> 0.8, \[Sigma] -> 1.1, \[Lambda] -> \
2.0, \[Eta] -> 0.6,\\n   \[Rho]0 -> 0, \[Chi]0 -> 1, r0 -> 0, s0 -> 0, Jobs \
-> 0\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ndispersion1D = dispersionDet /. {ky -> 0, kz \
-> 0, kx -> k} /. paramsNumeric // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nroots1D[kval_?NumericQ] := \\n  \[Omega] /. \
NSolve[(dispersion1D /. k -> kval) == 0, \[Omega], WorkingPrecision -> \
50];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsampleDispersionData = Table[\\n   {kv, roots1D[kv]},\
\\n   {kv, 0, 3, 0.1}\\n   ];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nflattenedRootData = Flatten[\
\\n   Table[{sampleDispersionData[[i, 1]], Re[#], Im[#]} & /@ \
sampleDispersionData[[i, 2]],\\n    {i, Length[sampleDispersionData]}], \
1];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nListPointPlot3D[\\n flattenedRootData,\\n AxesLabel -> \
{\\\"k\\\", \\\"Re[\[Omega]]\\\", \\\"Im[\[Omega]]\\\"},\\n PlotLabel -> \
\\\"Dispersion roots vs wave number\\\",\\n BoxRatios -> {1, 1, 0.7},\\n \
ImageSize -> Large\\n]\\n```\\n\\nThis quickly shows:\\n- real branches\\n- \
unstable branches with nonzero imaginary part\\n- \
degeneracies\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Finite-Domain PDE Eigenmode Test\\n\\nThis \
is where we test whether the linearized PDE actually supports stable spatial \
modes.\\n\\nWe first isolate one scalar prototype from the linearized system. \
If decoupling exists, use one mode directly; otherwise test a reduced \
operator.\\n\\n### Example scalar wave-mass operator\\n\\n```wl\\nreg = \
Rectangle[{0, 0}, {1, 1}];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nwaveMassVals = \
NDEigenvalues[\\n   {\\n    -Laplacian[\[Psi][x, y], {x, y}] + m2 \[Psi][x, \
y],\\n    DirichletCondition[\[Psi][x, y] == 0, True]\\n    },\\n   \[Psi][x, \
y], {x, y} \[Element] reg, 9,\\n   Method -> {\\\"FiniteElement\\\"}\\n   ] \
/. m2 -> 1.0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Finite-domain prototype eigenvalues:\
\\\"];\\nPrint[waveMassVals];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\n{evals, efuns} = \
NDEigensystem[\\n   {\\n    -Laplacian[\[Psi][x, y], {x, y}] + m2 \[Psi][x, \
y],\\n    DirichletCondition[\[Psi][x, y] == 0, True]\\n    },\\n   \[Psi][x, \
y], {x, y} \[Element] reg, 6,\\n   Method -> {\\\"FiniteElement\\\"}\\n   ] \
/. m2 -> 1.0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nGraphicsGrid[\\n Partition[\\n   Table[\\n   \
 ContourPlot[\\n     efuns[[i]][x, y], {x, 0, 1}, {y, 0, 1},\\n     \
PlotLegends -> Automatic,\\n     PlotLabel -> Row[{\\\"Mode \\\", i, \\\", \
\[Lambda] = \\\", NumberForm[evals[[i]], 6]}],\\n     ImageSize -> Medium\\n  \
   ],\\n    {i, Length[efuns]}\\n    ], 2, 2, {1, 1}, Nothing\\n   \
]\\n]\\n```\\n\\n### Why this matters\\n\\nIf you claim \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]stable geometry\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]allowed modes\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], bounded-domain \
eigensystems are a rigorous testbed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Time-Domain \
Simulation of a Reduced Mode\\n\\nA simple test of source-driven response:\\n\
\\n```wl\\nreducedEq = x''[t] + 2 \[Zeta] \[Omega]n x'[t] + \[Omega]n^2 x[t] \
== src[t];\\nsrc[t_] := Exp[-20 (t - 3)^2];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nreducedSol = \
NDSolveValue[\\n   {\\n    reducedEq /. {\[Zeta] -> 0.08, \[Omega]n -> \
2.5},\\n    x[0] == 0, x'[0] == 0\\n    },\\n   x, {t, 0, 10}\\n   \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nPlot[\\n {reducedSol[t], src[t]},\\n {t, 0, 10},\\n \
PlotLegends -> {\\\"mode response\\\", \\\"source\\\"},\\n PlotLabel -> \
\\\"Source-driven reduced mode\\\",\\n ImageSize -> Large\\n]\\n```\\n\\nThis \
is not yet the full OPF PDE evolution, but it gives a clean dynamical visual \
test.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Residual Testing\\n\\nAny claimed solution must \
satisfy the equations.\\n\\n```wl\\nresidualVector[\[Rho]cand_, \[Chi]cand_, \
rcand_, scand_] := \\n  FullSimplify[\\n   (SubtractSides /@ eulerBuiltIn) /. \
{\\n      \[Rho] -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Rho]cand],\\n      \[Chi] -> \
Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Chi]cand],\\n      r -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, \
zz}, rcand],\\n      s -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, scand]\\n      }\\n   ];\
\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ntrivialResidual = residualVector[0, 1, 0, \
0];\\nPrint[\\\"Residual for latent vacuum {0,1,0,0}: \\\", trivialResidual];\
\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsourceShiftResidual = residualVector[0, 1, 0, Jobs/\
\[Lambda]];\\nPrint[\\\"Residual for shifted s-background {0,1,0,Jobs/\
\[Lambda]}: \\\", sourceShiftResidual];\\n```\\n\\nIf the residual is not \
zero, the claimed background is not a solution.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. What \
Would Be Needed to Claim Specific Physics?\\n\\n### To claim a mode is \
light\\nNeed all of:\\n- massless branch\\n- Lorentz-consistent causal \
structure\\n- correct source coupling\\n- measurable field observables\\n- \
comparison to electromagnetic data\\n\\n### To claim a mode is sound\\nNeed \
all of:\\n- medium-dependent compressional mode\\n- subluminal group velocity\
\\n- pressure/density interpretation\\n- correct acoustic boundary \
behavior\\n\\n### To claim a mode is consciousness\\nNeed all of:\\n- \
independent operational definition\\n- nontrivial predictions not reducible \
to ordinary dynamics\\n- reproducible measurements\\n- falsifiable \
observer-dependent outcomes\\n\\nWithout that, the labels remain \
metaphoric.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Full Automated Test \
Report\\n\\n```wl\\ntestReport = <|\\n  \\\"EulerEquations\\\" -> \
eulerBuiltIn,\\n  \\\"BackgroundSystem\\\" -> backgroundSystem,\\n  \
\\\"BackgroundReduce\\\" -> backgroundReduce,\\n  \\\"BackgroundSolve\\\" -> \
backgroundSolve,\\n  \\\"PotentialHessian\\\" -> potentialHessian,\\n  \
\\\"HessianAtCandidate\\\" -> (potentialHessian /. candidateStationary),\\n  \
\\\"HessianEigenvaluesAtCandidate\\\" -> hessianEigenvalues,\\n  \
\\\"BackgroundTerms\\\" -> backgroundTerms,\\n  \\\"LinearTerms\\\" -> \
linearTerms,\\n  \\\"StiffnessMatrix\\\" -> stiffnessMatrix,\\n  \
\\\"DispersionDeterminant\\\" -> dispersionDet,\\n  \\\"BranchSolutions\\\" \
-> branchSolutions,\\n  \\\"BranchClassification\\\" -> branchClassification,\
\\n  \\\"TrivialResidual\\\" -> trivialResidual,\\n  \
\\\"SourceShiftResidual\\\" -> \
sourceShiftResidual\\n|>;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Automated test report:\\\
\"];\\nPrint[Dataset@testReport];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. Export the Audit \
Results\\n\\n```wl\\nExport[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\\\"opf-observer-rigorous-audit.wl\"\>",
                    Background->None,
                    FrameMargins->1,
                    FrameStyle->Dynamic[
                    CurrentValue[Background]],
                    StripOnInput->False], True->
                    FrameBox[
                    
                    StyleBox["\<\"# Rigorous Review and Test Harness for the \
Proposed OPF Observer Structure\\n\\nThis notebook does **not** assume the \
interpretation is correct. Instead, it turns the proposal into a \
**falsifiable, auditable test program**.\\n\\nIt separates:\\n\\n1. **what is \
mathematically derivable from the equations**\\n2. **what is an \
interpretation layered on top**\\n3. **what can be numerically tested \
here**\\n4. **what would require external data or independent validation**\\n\
\\nThe goal is to prevent category errors like:\\n- calling a mode \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] before proving \
Lorentz-consistent propagation\\n- calling a field \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]consciousness\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] before showing \
unique predictive content\\n- inferring lattice/CFL physics from a continuum \
Lagrangian without a discrete model\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 0. Review Summary: What \
Is Valid vs Not Yet Established\\n\\n### What is mathematically valid to test\
\\n\\nGiven a Lagrangian density of the \
form\\n\\n```wl\\nClearAll[\\\"Global`*\\\"];\\n$HistoryLength = \
0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncoords4 = {t, x, y, z};\\nspatialCoords = {x, y, \
z};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nlagrangianCandidate = \\n  \[Alpha]/2 Sum[D[\[Rho][t, \
x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] +\\n  \[Beta]/2 Sum[D[\[Chi][t, x, y, z], c]^2, \
{c, coords4}] +\\n  \[Mu]/2 Sum[D[r[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] +\\n  \
\[Sigma]/2 Sum[D[s[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, coords4}] -\\n  (\\n    \[Rho][t, \
x, y, z] Log[\[Chi][t, x, y, z]] +\\n    \[Chi][t, x, y, z] r[t, x, y, z]^2 +\
\\n    \[Lambda]/2 s[t, x, y, z]^2 -\\n    \[Eta] s[t, x, y, z] \[Rho][t, x, \
y, z]\\n  ) + Jobs s[t, x, y, z];\\n```\\n\\nyou can rigorously test:\\n\\n- \
Euler\[Dash]Lagrange equations\\n- constant-background existence \
conditions\\n- linearization around a background\\n- dispersion relations\\n- \
whether a mode is massless or massive\\n- whether propagation is \
hyperbolic/elliptic/unstable\\n- whether a finite-domain PDE has stable \
eigenmodes\\n\\n### What is **not** established by the equations \
alone\\n\\nThe following are **interpretive hypotheses**, not derived \
facts:\\n\\n- ``\[Rho]`` = thoughts\\n- ``r`` = light\\n- ``\[Chi]`` = \
sound/mechanical vibration\\n- ``s`` = consciousness\\n- ``c`` = CFL speed of \
a lattice\\n- \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]observer source\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
as physical consciousness\\n\\nThose claims require **extra predictive \
evidence**, not just symbolic resemblance.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Testing \
Philosophy\\n\\nWe will build a rigorous workflow with the following \
layers:\\n\\n### Layer A: Symbolic correctness\\n- derive equations in two \
ways\\n- verify sign consistency\\n- classify stationary backgrounds\\n\\n### \
Layer B: Spectral correctness\\n- compute stiffness matrix\\n- solve \
determinant conditions\\n- identify massless / massive branches\\n- test \
whether modes are real, damped, unstable, or tachyonic\\n\\n### Layer C: PDE \
correctness\\n- solve bounded-domain eigenproblems\\n- visualize \
eigenmodes\\n- compare operator forms\\n- measure residuals\\n\\n### Layer D: \
Dynamical correctness\\n- simulate time evolution\\n- test response to source \
pulses\\n- track conserved / nonconserved quantities where \
applicable\\n\\n### Layer E: Predictive discipline\\n- separate fit from \
forecast\\n- require out-of-sample agreement\\n- reject claims that are \
merely post hoc reinterpretations\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Initialization and \
Utilities\\n\\n```wl\\nNeeds[\\\"VariationalMethods`\\\"];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\\
n$Assumptions = \\n  Element[{\[Alpha], \[Beta], \[Mu], \[Sigma], \[Lambda], \
\[Eta], Jobs, \[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0, \[CurlyEpsilon], \[Omega], kx, ky, \
kz}, Reals] &&\\n   \[Alpha] > 0 && \[Beta] > 0 && \[Mu] > 0 && \[Sigma] > 0 \
&& \[Chi]0 > 0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncoords4 = {t, x, y, z};\\nspatialCoords = \
{x, y, z};\\nfields = {\[Rho], \[Chi], r, s};\\nfieldVars = Through[fields[t, \
x, y, z]];\\nkSq = kx^2 + ky^2 + kz^2;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[msg_] := \
Print[Style[msg, 14, Bold, Darker[Blue]]];\\npass[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"PASS: \\\" <> msg, Darker[Green]]];\\nfail[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"FAIL: \\\" <> msg, Red]];\\nwarn[msg_] := \
Print[Style[\\\"WARN: \\\" <> msg, \
Darker[Orange]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ntimeIt[label_, expr_] := Module[{tm, \
res},\\n  say[label];\\n  {tm, res} = AbsoluteTiming[expr];\\n  Print[Row[{\\\
\"Time: \\\", NumberForm[tm, {8, 4}], \\\" s\\\"}]];\\n  \
res\\n];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ngradMinkowskiSq[f_] := \\n  D[f[t, x, y, z], t]^2 \
- Sum[D[f[t, x, y, z], c]^2, {c, spatialCoords}];\\n\\nboxOp[f_] := D[f[t, x, \
y, z], {t, 2}] - Laplacian[f[t, x, y, z], \
spatialCoords];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Define the Candidate OPF Observer \
Lagrangian\\n\\n```wl\\npotential = \\n  \[Rho][t, x, y, z] Log[\[Chi][t, x, \
y, z]] +\\n  \[Chi][t, x, y, z] r[t, x, y, z]^2 +\\n  \[Lambda]/2 s[t, x, y, \
z]^2 -\\n  \[Eta] s[t, x, y, z] \[Rho][t, x, y, \
z];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nkinetic = \\n  \[Alpha]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[\[Rho]] +\\n \
 \[Beta]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[\[Chi]] +\\n  \[Mu]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[r] +\\n  \
\[Sigma]/2 gradMinkowskiSq[s];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nlagrangian = kinetic - \
potential + Jobs s[t, x, y, z];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Candidate \
Lagrangian defined.\\\"];\\nPrint[lagrangian // \
TraditionalForm];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Euler\[Dash]Lagrange Derivation \
and Cross-Check\\n\\n```wl\\neulerBuiltIn = EulerEquations[lagrangian, \
fieldVars, coords4] // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerExplicit = {\\n  \
 D[lagrangian, \[Rho][t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[\[Rho][t, x, y, \
z], c]], c] & /@ coords4],\\n   D[lagrangian, \[Chi][t, x, y, z]] - \
Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[\[Chi][t, x, y, z], c]], c] & /@ coords4],\\n   \
D[lagrangian, r[t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, D[r[t, x, y, z], c]], c] \
& /@ coords4],\\n   D[lagrangian, s[t, x, y, z]] - Total[D[D[lagrangian, \
D[s[t, x, y, z], c]], c] & /@ coords4]\\n   } // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerAudit = MapThread[FullSimplify[#1 == 0 \
/. Equal -> Subtract] &, {eulerBuiltIn - Thread[eulerExplicit == 0] /. Equal \
-> Subtract, ConstantArray[0, 4]}];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Euler \
equations from built-in variational \
derivation:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[eulerBuiltIn]];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Euler equations \
from explicit derivative form:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[Thread[eulerExplicit == \
0]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nIf[And @@ eulerAudit,\\n  pass[\\\"Built-in and \
explicit Euler\[Dash]Lagrange derivations agree.\\\"],\\n  \
fail[\\\"Variational derivations do not \
agree.\\\"]\\n];\\n```\\n\\n**Rigorous meaning:** if this fails, nothing \
downstream should be trusted.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Constant-Background \
Existence Test\\n\\nThis directly tests the claim that a nonzero constant \
observer source necessarily forbids a constant \
vacuum.\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundRules = {\\n   \[Rho][t, x, y, z] -> \
\[Rho]0,\\n   \[Chi][t, x, y, z] -> \[Chi]0,\\n   r[t, x, y, z] -> r0,\\n   \
s[t, x, y, z] -> s0,\\n   Derivative[__][\[Rho]][___] -> 0,\\n   \
Derivative[__][\[Chi]][___] -> 0,\\n   Derivative[__][r][___] -> 0,\\n   \
Derivative[__][s][___] -> 0\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundSystem = \
FullSimplify[(SubtractSides /@ eulerBuiltIn) /. backgroundRules == \
0];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Constant-background algebraic \
system:\\\"];\\nPrint[backgroundSystem // \
TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundReduce = Reduce[backgroundSystem, {\
\[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0}, Reals] // FullSimplify;\\nbackgroundSolve = \
Solve[backgroundSystem, {\[Rho]0, \[Chi]0, r0, s0}, Reals] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Constant-background \
classification:\\\"];\\nPrint[backgroundReduce // InputForm];\\n```\\n\\n### \
Interpretation rule\\n\\n- If ``Jobs > 0`` makes constant backgrounds \
impossible, then the correct statement is:\\n  - **this model does not admit \
a homogeneous static background with that source**\\n- It does **not** by \
itself prove consciousness or observer metaphysics\\n- It may suggest a \
forced inhomogeneous or time-dependent state\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Potential \
Hessian and Local Stability at a Candidate Background\\n\\nBefore calling \
anything \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]sound\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]observer\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], inspect the local \
quadratic form.\\n\\n```wl\\npotentialAlgebraic = \[Rho]s Log[\[Chi]s] + \
\[Chi]s rs^2 + \[Lambda]/2 ss^2 - \[Eta] ss \[Rho]s - Jobs ss;\\nvarsAlg = {\
\[Rho]s, \[Chi]s, rs, ss};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\npotentialGradient = \
Grad[potentialAlgebraic, varsAlg] // FullSimplify;\\npotentialHessian = \
D[potentialAlgebraic, {varsAlg, 2}] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ncandidateStationary = {\[Rho]s -> 0, \[Chi]s \
-> 1, rs -> 0, ss -> Jobs/\[Lambda]};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Potential \
gradient:\\\"];\\nPrint[potentialGradient // \
MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Potential Hessian:\\\"];\\nPrint[potentialHessian \
// MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Potential Hessian at candidate background:\\\"];\
\\nPrint[(potentialHessian /. candidateStationary) // \
MatrixForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nhessianEigenvalues = \
Eigenvalues[potentialHessian /. candidateStationary] // \
FullSimplify;\\nPrint[\\\"Hessian eigenvalues at candidate background: \\\", \
hessianEigenvalues];\\n```\\n\\n### Rigorous meaning\\n\\n- positive \
eigenvalues: locally stable directions\\n- zero eigenvalues: flat directions \
/ gauge / marginality\\n- negative eigenvalues: instability / tachyonic \
directions\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Linearization Around a Background\\n\\nWe \
linearize around a symbolic background:\\n\\n```wl\\nlinRules = {\\n   \[Rho] \
-> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Rho]0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] u[tt, xx, yy, \
zz]],\\n   \[Chi] -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Chi]0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
v[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\\n   r -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, r0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
w[tt, xx, yy, zz]],\\n   s -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, s0 + \[CurlyEpsilon] \
q[tt, xx, yy, zz]]\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\neulerLHS = SubtractSides /@ \
eulerBuiltIn;\\nbackgroundTerms = Normal[Series[#, {\[CurlyEpsilon], 0, 0}]] \
& /@ (eulerLHS /. linRules) // FullSimplify;\\nlinearTerms = \
Coefficient[Normal[Series[#, {\[CurlyEpsilon], 0, 1}]], \[CurlyEpsilon]] & /@ \
(eulerLHS /. linRules) // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Background \
terms:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[backgroundTerms]];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Linearized \
equations:\\\"];\\nPrint[Column[Thread[linearTerms == \
0]]];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbackgroundConsistency = \
FullSimplify[Thread[backgroundTerms == 0]];\\nPrint[\\\"Background \
consistency equations: \\\", backgroundConsistency];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \
8. Plane-Wave Reduction and Stiffness Matrix\\n\\nThis is the proper place to \
ask whether there are massless or massive branches.\\n\\n```wl\\nplaneRules = \
{\\n   u -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, u0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \
\[Omega] tt)]],\\n   v -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, v0 Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy \
+ kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\\n   w -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, w0 Exp[I (kx \
xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]],\\n   q -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, q0 \
Exp[I (kx xx + ky yy + kz zz - \[Omega] tt)]]\\n   \
};\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nmodalAlgebraic = FullSimplify[\\n   ((linearTerms /. \
planeRules) / Exp[I (kx x + ky y + kz z - \[Omega] t)])\\n   \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\namplitudes = {u0, v0, w0, q0};\\nstiffnessMatrix = \
Coefficient[#, amplitudes] & /@ modalAlgebraic // \
Simplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ndispersionDet = Det[stiffnessMatrix] // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Stiffness \
matrix:\\\"];\\nPrint[stiffnessMatrix // MatrixForm];\\n\\nsay[\\\"Dispersion \
determinant:\\\"];\\nPrint[dispersionDet // TraditionalForm];\\n```\\n\\n### \
Critical interpretation rule\\n\\nIf a branch gives\\n\\n$$\\n\\\\omega^2 = \
k^2\\n$$\\n\\nthen mathematically you have a **massless mode in the chosen \
normalization**.\\n\\nYou may only call it \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]light\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] if you additionally establish:\\n- correct Lorentz \
transformation structure\\n- correct coupling to matter/charge\\n- \
polarization structure if relevant\\n- agreement with measurable radiation \
phenomena\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Automated Branch \
Classification\\n\\n```wl\\nbranchSolutions = Solve[dispersionDet == 0, \
\[Omega]^2] // FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Solutions for \
\[Omega]^2:\\\"];\\nPrint[branchSolutions // \
TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nclassifyBranch[expr_] := Module[{e = \
FullSimplify[expr]},\\n  Which[\\n   FreeQ[e, kx | ky | kz], \\\"Pure gap / \
mass-only branch\\\",\\n   MatchQ[e, kSq], \\\"Massless branch\\\",\\n   \
MatchQ[e, kSq + _], \\\"Massive relativistic-like branch\\\",\\n   True, \
\\\"Mixed / coupled branch\\\"\\n   ]\\n  \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nbranchClassification = classifyBranch /@ (\[Omega]^2 /. \
branchSolutions);\\nPrint[Transpose[{\[Omega]^2 /. branchSolutions, \
branchClassification}] // TableForm];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Visual \
Parameter Exploration of Dispersion Branches\\n\\nTo make this runnable with \
visuals, fix a 1D wavevector ``k``.\\n\\n```wl\\nparamsNumeric = {\\n   \
\[Alpha] -> 1, \[Beta] -> 1.3, \[Mu] -> 0.8, \[Sigma] -> 1.1, \[Lambda] -> \
2.0, \[Eta] -> 0.6,\\n   \[Rho]0 -> 0, \[Chi]0 -> 1, r0 -> 0, s0 -> 0, Jobs \
-> 0\\n   };\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ndispersion1D = dispersionDet /. {ky -> 0, kz \
-> 0, kx -> k} /. paramsNumeric // \
FullSimplify;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nroots1D[kval_?NumericQ] := \\n  \[Omega] /. \
NSolve[(dispersion1D /. k -> kval) == 0, \[Omega], WorkingPrecision -> \
50];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsampleDispersionData = Table[\\n   {kv, roots1D[kv]},\
\\n   {kv, 0, 3, 0.1}\\n   ];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nflattenedRootData = Flatten[\
\\n   Table[{sampleDispersionData[[i, 1]], Re[#], Im[#]} & /@ \
sampleDispersionData[[i, 2]],\\n    {i, Length[sampleDispersionData]}], \
1];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nListPointPlot3D[\\n flattenedRootData,\\n AxesLabel -> \
{\\\"k\\\", \\\"Re[\[Omega]]\\\", \\\"Im[\[Omega]]\\\"},\\n PlotLabel -> \
\\\"Dispersion roots vs wave number\\\",\\n BoxRatios -> {1, 1, 0.7},\\n \
ImageSize -> Large\\n]\\n```\\n\\nThis quickly shows:\\n- real branches\\n- \
unstable branches with nonzero imaginary part\\n- \
degeneracies\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Finite-Domain PDE Eigenmode Test\\n\\nThis \
is where we test whether the linearized PDE actually supports stable spatial \
modes.\\n\\nWe first isolate one scalar prototype from the linearized system. \
If decoupling exists, use one mode directly; otherwise test a reduced \
operator.\\n\\n### Example scalar wave-mass operator\\n\\n```wl\\nreg = \
Rectangle[{0, 0}, {1, 1}];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nwaveMassVals = \
NDEigenvalues[\\n   {\\n    -Laplacian[\[Psi][x, y], {x, y}] + m2 \[Psi][x, \
y],\\n    DirichletCondition[\[Psi][x, y] == 0, True]\\n    },\\n   \[Psi][x, \
y], {x, y} \[Element] reg, 9,\\n   Method -> {\\\"FiniteElement\\\"}\\n   ] \
/. m2 -> 1.0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Finite-domain prototype eigenvalues:\
\\\"];\\nPrint[waveMassVals];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\n{evals, efuns} = \
NDEigensystem[\\n   {\\n    -Laplacian[\[Psi][x, y], {x, y}] + m2 \[Psi][x, \
y],\\n    DirichletCondition[\[Psi][x, y] == 0, True]\\n    },\\n   \[Psi][x, \
y], {x, y} \[Element] reg, 6,\\n   Method -> {\\\"FiniteElement\\\"}\\n   ] \
/. m2 -> 1.0;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nGraphicsGrid[\\n Partition[\\n   Table[\\n   \
 ContourPlot[\\n     efuns[[i]][x, y], {x, 0, 1}, {y, 0, 1},\\n     \
PlotLegends -> Automatic,\\n     PlotLabel -> Row[{\\\"Mode \\\", i, \\\", \
\[Lambda] = \\\", NumberForm[evals[[i]], 6]}],\\n     ImageSize -> Medium\\n  \
   ],\\n    {i, Length[efuns]}\\n    ], 2, 2, {1, 1}, Nothing\\n   \
]\\n]\\n```\\n\\n### Why this matters\\n\\nIf you claim \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]stable geometry\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] or \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]allowed modes\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], bounded-domain \
eigensystems are a rigorous testbed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Time-Domain \
Simulation of a Reduced Mode\\n\\nA simple test of source-driven response:\\n\
\\n```wl\\nreducedEq = x''[t] + 2 \[Zeta] \[Omega]n x'[t] + \[Omega]n^2 x[t] \
== src[t];\\nsrc[t_] := Exp[-20 (t - 3)^2];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nreducedSol = \
NDSolveValue[\\n   {\\n    reducedEq /. {\[Zeta] -> 0.08, \[Omega]n -> \
2.5},\\n    x[0] == 0, x'[0] == 0\\n    },\\n   x, {t, 0, 10}\\n   \
];\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nPlot[\\n {reducedSol[t], src[t]},\\n {t, 0, 10},\\n \
PlotLegends -> {\\\"mode response\\\", \\\"source\\\"},\\n PlotLabel -> \
\\\"Source-driven reduced mode\\\",\\n ImageSize -> Large\\n]\\n```\\n\\nThis \
is not yet the full OPF PDE evolution, but it gives a clean dynamical visual \
test.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Residual Testing\\n\\nAny claimed solution must \
satisfy the equations.\\n\\n```wl\\nresidualVector[\[Rho]cand_, \[Chi]cand_, \
rcand_, scand_] := \\n  FullSimplify[\\n   (SubtractSides /@ eulerBuiltIn) /. \
{\\n      \[Rho] -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Rho]cand],\\n      \[Chi] -> \
Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, \[Chi]cand],\\n      r -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, \
zz}, rcand],\\n      s -> Function[{tt, xx, yy, zz}, scand]\\n      }\\n   ];\
\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\ntrivialResidual = residualVector[0, 1, 0, \
0];\\nPrint[\\\"Residual for latent vacuum {0,1,0,0}: \\\", trivialResidual];\
\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsourceShiftResidual = residualVector[0, 1, 0, Jobs/\
\[Lambda]];\\nPrint[\\\"Residual for shifted s-background {0,1,0,Jobs/\
\[Lambda]}: \\\", sourceShiftResidual];\\n```\\n\\nIf the residual is not \
zero, the claimed background is not a solution.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. What \
Would Be Needed to Claim Specific Physics?\\n\\n### To claim a mode is \
light\\nNeed all of:\\n- massless branch\\n- Lorentz-consistent causal \
structure\\n- correct source coupling\\n- measurable field observables\\n- \
comparison to electromagnetic data\\n\\n### To claim a mode is sound\\nNeed \
all of:\\n- medium-dependent compressional mode\\n- subluminal group velocity\
\\n- pressure/density interpretation\\n- correct acoustic boundary \
behavior\\n\\n### To claim a mode is consciousness\\nNeed all of:\\n- \
independent operational definition\\n- nontrivial predictions not reducible \
to ordinary dynamics\\n- reproducible measurements\\n- falsifiable \
observer-dependent outcomes\\n\\nWithout that, the labels remain \
metaphoric.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Full Automated Test \
Report\\n\\n```wl\\ntestReport = <|\\n  \\\"EulerEquations\\\" -> \
eulerBuiltIn,\\n  \\\"BackgroundSystem\\\" -> backgroundSystem,\\n  \
\\\"BackgroundReduce\\\" -> backgroundReduce,\\n  \\\"BackgroundSolve\\\" -> \
backgroundSolve,\\n  \\\"PotentialHessian\\\" -> potentialHessian,\\n  \
\\\"HessianAtCandidate\\\" -> (potentialHessian /. candidateStationary),\\n  \
\\\"HessianEigenvaluesAtCandidate\\\" -> hessianEigenvalues,\\n  \
\\\"BackgroundTerms\\\" -> backgroundTerms,\\n  \\\"LinearTerms\\\" -> \
linearTerms,\\n  \\\"StiffnessMatrix\\\" -> stiffnessMatrix,\\n  \
\\\"DispersionDeterminant\\\" -> dispersionDet,\\n  \\\"BranchSolutions\\\" \
-> branchSolutions,\\n  \\\"BranchClassification\\\" -> branchClassification,\
\\n  \\\"TrivialResidual\\\" -> trivialResidual,\\n  \
\\\"SourceShiftResidual\\\" -> \
sourceShiftResidual\\n|>;\\n```\\n\\n```wl\\nsay[\\\"Automated test report:\\\
\"];\\nPrint[Dataset@testReport];\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. Export the Audit \
Results\\n\\n```wl\\nExport[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\\\"opf-observer-rigorous-audit.wl\"\>",
                    StripOnInput->False,
                    FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
                    Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1],
                    FrameMargins->1,
                    FrameStyle->Dynamic[
                    CurrentValue[Background]],
                    StripOnInput->False]}, Dynamic[
                    CurrentValue["MouseOver"]],
                    FrameMargins->0,
                    ImageSize->Automatic],
                    MouseAppearanceTag["LinkHand"]],
                    
                    EventHandlerTag[{
                    "MouseEntered" :> (
                    Wolfram`Chatbook`ResourceFunctions`ClickToCopy`cell$$ = 
                    FrontEndExecute[
                    FrontEnd`AttachCell[
                    EvaluationBox[], 
                    Cell[
                    BoxData[
                    GraphicsBox[{
                    FaceForm[
                    RGBColor[
                    0.9607843137254902, 0.9607843137254902, 
                    0.9607843137254902]], 
                    EdgeForm[
                    RGBColor[
                    0.8980392156862745, 0.8980392156862745, 
                    0.8980392156862745]], 
                    RectangleBox[{-18, 0}, {18, 8}, RoundingRadius -> 0.5], 
                    InsetBox[
                    BoxData[
                    FormBox[
                    StyleBox[
                    TagBox[
                    GridBox[{{
                    GraphicsBox[{
                    RGBColor[
                    0.5372549019607843, 0.5372549019607843, 
                    0.5372549019607843], 
