           "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<The Log[\[Chi]] structure is a KL-divergence-like scale\n\
   anomaly      (F7, F10). It gives \[Chi] a flat direction: the Hessian at \
(0,1,0) has eigenvalues {2,1,0}\n        and the zero eigenvalue is along \
\[Chi] itself. Scale is literally the unmeasured\n   dimension.\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<F7 (Log[\[Chi]] is the uncancellable scale-anomaly\n  \
 direction)\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<F10 (KL potential, exactly 1-homogeneous, flat along\n  \
 \[Chi])\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<r (radial curvature)\>\"", "->", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<ontology\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<radial geometric mode; coupling between coherence and\n  \
 curvature\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<intuitiveShorthand\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<the toroidal winding tension\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<modernAnalogs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<Ricci scalar R in Einstein-Hilbert\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<radial coordinate in spherical PDE reduction\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<order parameter in Landau theory\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<Enters as \[Chi] r^2 -- the ONLY coupling between \[Chi] \
and\n   r.      This is what makes r=0 the trivial stable point: no linear \
tadpole, pure quadratic.      Mapping to Einstein-Hilbert is role-analogous, \
not quantitative -- there is no metric\n   here.\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<F2 (r=0 at trivial fixed point)\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<F4 (saddle-node theorem: nontrivial branch at \[Lambda]\
\n   \[LessEqual] e/8)\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<\[CapitalGamma] (maintenance decay)\>\"", "->", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<ontology\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<decay rate of unmeasured / unsupported state\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<intuitiveShorthand\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<the forgetting constant\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<modernAnalogs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<damping ratio 2\[Zeta]\[Omega]n in DampedOscillator\>\
\"", ",", "\"\<dissipation \[Kappa] in HeatEquation\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<Lindblad decay rate in open quantum systems\>\""}], 
           "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<AS WRITTEN the maintenance law is pure decay -- \[Phi] \
\[Rule]\n   0.      F8 showed this is NOT persistence: you need the pitchfork \
fix      d u/dt = -\[CapitalGamma] u + g tanh(u), which has a nontrivial \
fixed point iff\n   g/\[CapitalGamma] > 1.      The current notebook's \
section 14 only shows the decay half.\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{
          "{", "\"\<F8 (pitchfork fix persists iff g/\[CapitalGamma] > 1; u* \
=\n   0.1734 at 1.01)\>\"", "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<\[Alpha], \[Beta], \[Mu] (regularizers)\>\"", "->", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<ontology\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<spatial-coherence stiffness coefficients for \[Rho], \
\[Chi],\n   r\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<intuitiveShorthand\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<resistance to local variation\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<modernAnalogs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<kinetic coefficients in Lagrangian field theory\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<diffusion constants D in reaction-diffusion\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<elastic moduli in continuum mechanics\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<SIGNATURE-DEPENDENT. With Euclidean gradSq4 (as \
written):      these are diffusion constants and the system maps to \
Heat/Poisson/ReactionDiffusion.      With Lorentzian gradSqMinkowski \
(commented in section 1): these are wave speeds squared      and the system \
maps to Wave/KleinGordon. Pick one and commit.\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{
          "{", "\"\<F19-F21 (notebook linearization and dispersion fixes)\>\"",
            "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Confidence Corridor CI\>\"", "->", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<ontology\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<stability band for self-measurement; STRESS when \
CI_lower <\n   \[Phi]^-1\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<intuitiveShorthand\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<the resonance pocket the system falls into\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<modernAnalogs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<Lyapunov function level set\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<conformal prediction interval\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<basin of attraction boundary\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<NOT derivable from the Lagrangian. The Corridor is an    \
  operational-learning construct bolted on at the self-measurement layer.     \
 Treating it as emerging from the field equations is a category error.\>\""}],
          ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<F17 (AdaptiveConformal holds 0.90 coverage through 3\
\[Times]\n   drift)\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<F18 (corridor inverted 30.9%, severity saturates at\n   \
\[Phi]^-2)\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<\[Phi]-scaling (golden ratio)\>\"", "->", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<ontology\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<self-similar scaling across octaves of structure\>\""}], 
         ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<intuitiveShorthand\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<the universe's packing constant\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<modernAnalogs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<Vogel spiral discrepancy\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<Diophantine continued-fraction score\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<quasi-crystal diffraction spacing\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<VERIFIED CLAIMS: wins packing (Vogel 0.38200 vs 0.38197) \
and      non-resonance (CF score 5.5 vs \[Pi]'s 3.3244).      UNVERIFIED \
CLAIMS: everything else. \[Phi]-ablations never help in F15's omega library\n \
  audit.      Do not use \[Phi]-scaling to justify a mapping unless F11 or \
F27 covers it.\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<F11 (packing/non-resonance only)\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<F27 (self-measurement conjugate widths      sx \
\[CenterDot] \[Phi]^(-n/2), s\[Sigma] \[CenterDot] \[Phi]^(+n/2))\>\""}], 
           "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<self-measurement spectrum\>\"", "->", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<ontology\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<\[Lambda](k,q) = \[Lambda]x \[CenterDot] \[Lambda]\
\[Sigma];      persistence is 2\[Pi] sx s\[Sigma] = 1\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<intuitiveShorthand\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<position-scale uncertainty pair\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<modernAnalogs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<Heisenberg conjugate uncertainty\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<Fourier dual-scale invariance\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<wavelet admissibility\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<The quantization 2\[Pi] sx s\[Sigma] = 1 is a genuine\n  \
 conservation law      of the self-measurement operator (F5). It is the \
strongest cross-scale invariant verified\n   so far.      Numerical anchor: \
\[Lambda](0.7, 0.3) = 0.954894005662 on the critical band.\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<F5 (persistence quantization)\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<F27 (survives all scales under \[Phi]-dilation)\>\""}], 
           "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<trivial fixed point (0, 1, 0)\>\"", "->", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<ontology\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<the vacuum of empty measurement\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<intuitiveShorthand\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<nothing measuring nothing, with unit ruler\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<modernAnalogs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<false vacuum in SSB potentials\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<unstable equilibrium in dynamical systems\>\""}], 
           "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<SADDLE, not minimum (F2: det H = -2 for ALL parameter \
values).\n        The system cannot rest here -- it must either decay (F8 \
without pitchfork) or lift to      the nontrivial branch (F4: exists iff \
\[Lambda] \[LessEqual] e/8). The notebook returning      {\[Rho]=0, \[Chi]=1, \
r=0} as 'the solution' is formally correct but physically marginal.\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<F2 (saddle, det H = -2)\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<F3 (gradient ascent unstable \[ForAll] r; Newton \
converges)\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<F4 (saddle-node fold at (e/8, 4/e, e, -2/e))\>\""}], 
           "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<nontrivial branch\>\"", "->", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<ontology\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<the first non-vacuum stable configuration\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<intuitiveShorthand\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<the first brick that stands\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<modernAnalogs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<true vacuum after SSB\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<nontrivial fixed point in RG flow\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<mappingNotes\>\"", 
          "->", "\"\<Exists iff \[Lambda] \[LessEqual] e/8 \[TildeTilde] \
0.3398.      Fold at (\[Lambda], \[Rho]*, \[Chi]*, r*) = (e/8, 4/e, e, -2/e) \
= (0.3398, 1.4715, 2.7183,\n   -1.3591).      Still a SADDLE (mixed-sign \
Hessian) -- not a minimum. True stability requires the      pitchfork fix at \
the maintenance layer.\>\""}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<verifiedBy\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<F2 (nontrivial branch is also saddle)\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<F4 (closed-form saddle-node, engine-confirmed)\>\""}], 
           "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
